body:
Created by **Nicolas Hachet**, 31st Aug 2013. _(originally [Lighthouse ticket #4035](http://cakephp.lighthouseapp.com/projects/42648/tickets/4035))_:

---
#### Context

CakePHP 2.3.10
PHP 5.3.13
Apache 2.2.22
#### What I did

I would to validate multiple rows using Model :: validateMany().
#### What happened

With options "deep" set to false, $this -> request -> data is modified incorrectly (a model key is added).
With options "deep" set to true, the result is as expected ($this -> request -> data didn't change).

Here is a test code :

``` php
// IN
debug($this -> request -> data);
$this -> Order -> set($this -> request -> data);
if ($this -> Order -> validates() 
    && $this -> Participant -> validateMany($this -> request -> data['Participant'])) { // Didn't work
    //&& $this -> Participant -> validateMany($this -> request -> data['Participant'], array('deep' => true))) { // Work
    // Saving stuff... 
} else {
    $this -> Session -> setFlash(__('Please correct displayed errors.'), 'default', array(
        'class' => 'warning'
    ));
}
// OUT
debug($this -> request -> data); 
```

Output :

``` php
// IN
array(
    'Order' => array(
        'id' => '',
        // ...
    ),
    'Participant' => array(
        (int) 0 => array(
            'firstname' => 'test',
            'lastname' => '',
            'mail' => ''
        ),
        (int) 1 => array(
            'firstname' => '',
            'lastname' => 'test',
            'mail' => ''
        )
    )
)
// OUT
array(
    'Order' => array(
        'id' => '',
        // ...
    ),
    'Participant' => array(
        (int) 0 => array(
            'Participant' => array(
                'firstname' => 'test',
                'lastname' => '',
                'mail' => ''
            )
        ),
        (int) 1 => array(
            'Participant' => array(
                'firstname' => '',
                'lastname' => 'test',
                'mail' => ''
            )
        )
    )
)
```
#### What I expected to happen

Model::validateMany shouldn't modify $this -> request -> data with "deep" set to false (default behaviour).
#### Code of ModelValidator::validateMany

Row 211

``` php
if ($options['deep']) {
    $validates = $model->validateAssociated($record, $options);
} else {
    $model->create(null);
    $validates = $model->set($record) && $model->validates($options);
    $data[$key] = $model->data;
}
```
